# Legion round 6 (2026-10-21): a second gatehouse, not the first's copy. The target stands in a walled yard (1-cell
# walls, 6-7 cells out) open on the NORTH through a 4-cell gap; round it runs a 4-CELL corridor inside an outer wall
# entered by two gates, one on the west (group A, 24 attackers with 2x2 footprints) and one on the south (group B,
# 12 with 3x3 footprints), both with range 160. A 3x3 body is single file in the corridor, a 2x2 one has two lanes
# when the first stands against a wall and none when it stands in the middle. Bodies get the shot flush with the
# yard's walls (the sight cast skips the cells beside a big body) and through the north gap; the rest of reach is
# shadow. Built to check that the walk on past the shot (walkOnShot) fills a corridor deep-first for another width,
# gate layout and footprint mix than attackring-gatehouse-40.
name attackring-gateyard-36
ticks 3000
seed 7
players 2
